codex
I found a gap in the new ambiguity check: it checks exclusive groups, but not the existing rule that a premise can have only one membership for the same place and axis. An overlapping void and replacement could therefore return the same district twice, or return both “within” and “outside” for one city. I’m writing a rollback-only probe to test both cases.
