- **A short round 5 before the mirror (Ryan, 2026-11-06: "do the short round 5"), though all three reviewers were ready on r4.** *Why:* `tu.sql` is append-only, so a comment that misstates what the database does (Codex r4 S1: `cash_drawn_at`'s source term is not always 0 at a take-back's instant) would stay in the permanent schema; and Opus r4 S1's wrong retry hint was cheap to fix. *Why not mirror r4 and carry the items:* a later patch could only add a correction beside the wrong comment.
